<title>UK: Lonrho director Wadeson resigns.</title>
<headline>Lonrho director Wadeson resigns.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lonrho Plc said non-executive director T.C.A. Wadeson has stepped down after shareholder Anglo American Corp of South Africa Ltd last week promised his resignation to the European Commission.</p>
<p>The promise was part of the deal under which Anglo agreed to trim its stake in Lonrho to overcome EU worries that the South African company would otherwise get a too dominant position on world platinum markets.</p>
<p>Wadeson, who was appointed as director in May 1996, was Anglo's nominee on the Lonrho board.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
